# OS-package CVEs accepted for the API runtime image.
#
# Read by the `Scan the image for OS vulnerabilities` step of the `image` job in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml. That scan covers ONLY what arrives with node:22-alpine — alpine,
# musl, busybox, openssl, curl. The npm dependency tree is gated separately by
# `pnpm audit:ci`, which has its own triage file with mandatory reasons and expiry dates
# (.github/audit-allowlist.json).
#
# Two scanners over one tree with two different mute mechanisms means a finding silenced in
# one place still reds the build in the other, and the fix nobody has time for is to mute it
# twice. Keeping the boundary at "OS packages here, npm packages there" is what avoids that.
#
# The scan already passes --ignore-unfixed, so anything reaching this file has a FIX
# available and is being accepted anyway. That should be rare and always temporary: the
# normal response to a fixable HIGH in the base image is to rebuild against a newer
# node:22-alpine, which Dependabot proposes weekly (.github/dependabot.yml).
#
# Format — one CVE id per line, with the justification and a review date above it:
#
#   # CVE-2025-00000 (openssl) — not reachable: the API makes no outbound TLS connection
#   # from this path, and alpine has not shipped the fix to the 3.21 branch yet.
#   # Review by 2026-12-01.
#   CVE-2025-00000
#
# Empty is the correct state. Adding an entry is a decision that belongs in a reviewed diff,
# not a way to get a red build green.
